  "gaps": [
    "Birth year is disputed: 1314 (age 78 in the Life; Borisov) or 1322 (earlier line, about 70; Kuchkin, Kloss); Nikon’s 19th-c. Life gives 1319. birth_year is left null under the Directus rule for disputed dates.",
    "Life chapters 14–15, 17–20, 23–24, 27–30, and the posthumous miracles in 34–88 were not read in detail. The miracles list therefore summarizes chs. 34–88 from chapter titles only, and the founding chapters for Kirzhach, Andronikov, Simonov, Golutvin, and Vysoky are named but not told.",
    "The claim that the Roman martyrology added Sergius in 1969 rests only on Russian Wikipedia and is left out; feast_day_catholic is null and venerated_in is orthodox only. A Catholic primary source could change this.",
    "The hill name “Makovets” and the founding date of the Trinity monastery (1337 or 1342) are not in the sources read and are not stated.",
    "The Kulikovo link, the year 1380, and the monks Peresvet and Oslyabya come from the later Tale of the Mamai Rout, which was not itself read; the biography attributes them. Kuchkin’s link to the Vozha (1378) is given as a scholar’s view.",
    "The birds vision was read only in Dimitry of Rostov’s Life (S2) and is attributed to it.",
    "Varnitsy as birthplace rests on Russian Wikipedia; the Life says only a village in the Rostov principality.",
    "The head-switch story (Florensky, Olsufiev) is church tradition; the 1919 protocol reports bones of the whole body. Both are given.",
    "Only 4 block quotes in the biography (aim 6–12): the Life is available only in a modern translation marked facts-only, which allows at most two short block quotes, and the only public-domain wording in the notes is Rogovich 1922.",
    "Only 3 quote records (aim 10–30): the notes hold few exact words of Sergius himself; most of his recorded sayings are marked as paraphrases and cannot be quoted.",
    "Biography is 5,037 words, at the floor of tier B; the notes do not support more without padding.",
    "Unopened Sanidopoulos pages (relics uncovering 1422; miracles of Sergius and Nikon; resource page), pravenc.ru, drevo-info, and the Great Menaion Reader text could add posthumous miracles and quotations.",
    "Disciples named as saints (Nikon, Savva, Andronikus, Micah, Athanasius of Serpukhov) come from the Sanidopoulos label list and were not read."
